`check face` judges a router's config file against the constrained faces
its face policy names (`link.v1` §2.15, #769). What a router runs is not on
the bus (core §11.3), so it reads a file, through zenoh's own loader, and
opens no session. For each face it reads the block as it guards the far
side: the denies of every policy whose subject can match the far
principal's sessions, subject by subject, since any allow wins across
subjects (§2.4), and the downsampling rules on the face's transports. Then
it compares the whole block with the plan the same face policy, enrollment
and contracts compile to, as `acl gen --check` does.

The lab router of `examples/zk2/link/`, running the block `acl gen
--face-policy` wrote: every face guarded as planned, exit 0. The windows
were not asked, and the note says so.

```console
$ zenctl check face tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router.json5 --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml --enrollment ../examples/zk2/link/radio.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/link/radio.v1.toml --format table
tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router.json5: face radio (far ground): 8 deny rule(s) across subject(s) ground; 2 downsampling rule(s) on its transports
PASS
judged against the config file tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router.json5 through zenoh's own loader: what a router runs is not observable on the bus, so a file that differs from what it was started with is invisible here (core §11.3, link.v1 §2.14)
tombstone windows not asked: pass --window ADDRESS=SECS for each listed owner of state (link.v1 §2.11)

```

The same block hand-edited the two ways a deployment must not: the `zk`
deny taken out of ground's policy, and one wildcard rule in place of the
two (scenarios §3, step 2). Both are §2.15's findings, and the comparison
names the edits. Exit 1.

```console
$ zenctl check face tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router-drifted.json5 --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml --enrollment ../examples/zk2/link/radio.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/link/radio.v1.toml --format table
? 1
tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router-drifted.json5: face radio (far ground): 7 deny rule(s) across subject(s) ground; 1 downsampling rule(s) on its transports
  ✗ zk_not_denied          face radio  @zk
  ✗ wildcard_downsampling  face radio  zk2/lab/*/radio.v1/stream/air/dropped_total
against the plan: 3 difference(s)
  ✗ policy_missing        ground  planned rules [call-in:tool.console, call-out:tool.console, consume-in:tool.console, consume-out:tool.console, face:radio:@state, face:radio:@stream:radio.v1, face:radio:admin, face:radio:adv, face:radio:events:radio.v1, face:radio:state:radio.v1, face:radio:stream:radio.v1, face:radio:zk] subjects [ground]
  ✗ policy_extra          ground  configured rules [call-in:tool.console, call-out:tool.console, consume-in:tool.console, consume-out:tool.console, face:radio:@state, face:radio:@stream:radio.v1, face:radio:admin, face:radio:adv, face:radio:events:radio.v1, face:radio:state:radio.v1, face:radio:stream:radio.v1] subjects [ground]
  ✗ downsampling_differs  radio   planned link_protocols unixsock-stream egress put zk2/lab/radio-a/radio.v1/@stream/frames@1Hz zk2/lab/radio-a/radio.v1/stream/air/dropped_total@1Hz; configured link_protocols unixsock-stream egress put zk2/lab/*/radio.v1/stream/air/dropped_total@1Hz
FAIL
zk_not_denied [face radio] @zk: a pair of the nine messages and both flows is not denied on @zk: presence, descriptors or bundles cross the face (§2.6, §2.15)
wildcard_downsampling [face radio] zk2/lab/*/radio.v1/stream/air/dropped_total: a downsampling rule that is not one concrete key: every key it covers shares one timer (§2.8, §2.15)
judged against the config file tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router-drifted.json5 through zenoh's own loader: what a router runs is not observable on the bus, so a file that differs from what it was started with is invisible here (core §11.3, link.v1 §2.14)
tombstone windows not asked: pass --window ADDRESS=SECS for each listed owner of state (link.v1 §2.11)

```

Given the windows the deployment configures (§2.11), every listed owner of
state is checked against each face's outage, a window not given being the
core's 60 s. A window of 2 s below the radio face's 6 s outage is a
finding, though the block itself is clean.

```console
$ zenctl check face tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router.json5 --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml --enrollment ../examples/zk2/link/radio.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/link/radio.v1.toml --window lab/radio-a=2 --format ndjson
? 1
{"against":"tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router.json5","comparison":{"answer":"not_established","reason":"tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router.json5 carries the plan whole: 26 rule(s), 5 subject(s), 5 polic(y/ies), enabled, default deny, 1 downsampling item(s)"},"judgement":{"answer":"established"},"namespace":"","notes":[{"text":"window_under_outage [face radio] lab/radio-a: a listed owner of state's tombstone window is below the face's outage: a delete made during a longer outage is lost across the face (§2.11)"},{"cite":"core §11.3, link.v1 §2.14","text":"judged against the config file tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router.json5 through zenoh's own loader: what a router runs is not observable on the bus, so a file that differs from what it was started with is invisible here"},{"text":"the windows are the ones given: whether each owner runs with its window is its configuration, not on the bus (link.v1 §2.11, §5)"}],"report":"face-check"}
{"denies":8,"face":"radio","far":"ground","row":"face","rules":2,"subjects":["ground"]}
{"at":"lab/radio-a","code":"window_under_outage","face":"radio","row":"finding","severity":"error"}
{"face":"radio","given":true,"min_s":6,"row":"window","service":"lab/radio-a","window_s":2}
window_under_outage [face radio] lab/radio-a: a listed owner of state's tombstone window is below the face's outage: a delete made during a longer outage is lost across the face (§2.11)
judged against the config file tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router.json5 through zenoh's own loader: what a router runs is not observable on the bus, so a file that differs from what it was started with is invisible here (core §11.3, link.v1 §2.14)
the windows are the ones given: whether each owner runs with its window is its configuration, not on the bus (link.v1 §2.11, §5)

```

A file that is not there, and a window that is not `ADDRESS=SECS`, are
questions that could not be asked: exit 2, never a 1 claiming the router
guards its faces wrongly.

```console
$ zenctl check face tests/cmd/fixtures/link/no-such-router.json5 --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml --enrollment ../examples/zk2/link/radio.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/link/radio.v1.toml
? 2
Error: tests/cmd/fixtures/link/no-such-router.json5: zenoh refused the config: No such file or directory (os error 2)
check face: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```

```console
$ zenctl check face tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router.json5 --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml --enrollment ../examples/zk2/link/radio.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/link/radio.v1.toml --window radio-a=2
? 2
Error: --window "radio-a=2": "radio-a" is not <system>/<service>: "radio-a" is not a zk2 key: an address is <system>/<service>
check face: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```

A face policy its linter refuses has no plan, and no block is judged
against it: exit 2.

```console
$ zenctl check face tests/cmd/fixtures/link/router.json5 --face-policy tests/cmd/fixtures/link/radio-router.face.toml --enrollment ../examples/zk2/link/radio.enrollment.toml --contracts ../examples/zk2/link/radio.v1.toml
? 2
Error: --face-policy: the face policy is refused (link.v1 §2.1): error router_attach [face radio] attach. Router to router is refused (§8.5, §11.3: on a router-to-router link, a deny hides a denied declaration from the far side, but its key string still crosses (spike S3: 11,330 B and 201 denied keys, against 506 B and none in a south region)): attach the far router in a south region (attach = "south-region", region = "<name>"), or the far session as a client (attach = "client")
check face: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```
